Z||000006||ChadMan||03-09-2000||09:59 AM||||Hey DarkLord, if you're looking for plain wheels, the 15x6 stamped steel wheels from 1995-2000 Cavaliers/Sunfires/Grand Ams/etc have the correct bolt pattern, and there are lots of cool Pontiac wheel covers that will fit them.  Not sure what the offset is though.||||reg||1
Z||000007||william_thorniii||03-09-2000||01:05 PM||||Darklord,<P>Have you checked your area for used Fiero wheels?  I got my "Turbo" rims for $25 ea.  I only had to get the tires re-mounted.  Lots of Fiero-folks have at least one extra set of turbo's that they wouldn't mind parting with.  <P>...Or if you are interested, I have the factory steel 13" with Gold Tri-Tech covers.  The covers are in good shape and paintable.  They looked decent (better than newer style covers.  I would be willing to sell these if you want.  Don't worry either, I won't charge the $2XX that the dealership does.  LOL<P>Let me know,<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
